# Who reviews what (GitHub requests their review on a pull request that touches it).
# CI, the test catalog, the selector and the solution and build roots decide what every later change
# is tested by, and a change to any of them runs the whole ring (ci.yml's whole-ring step), so it
# is a workflow change and needs the owner's review (#487). Keep this in step with that list.
/.github/                         @danswett
/quality/                         @danswett
/tools/AgentBridge.Quality/       @danswett
/tests/AgentBridge.Quality.Tests/ @danswett
/build/                           @danswett
# CODEOWNERS paths are case sensitive, while the whole-ring step and the tools aren't (NuGet on
# Linux loads NuGet.Config too, and MSBuild on Windows any case), so each spelling they load is here.
Directory.*.props                 @danswett
Directory.*.targets               @danswett
directory.*.props                 @danswett
directory.*.targets               @danswett
*.sln                             @danswett
*.slnx                            @danswett
global.json                       @danswett
Global.json                       @danswett
nuget.config                      @danswett
NuGet.config                      @danswett
NuGet.Config                      @danswett
Nuget.config                      @danswett
